{# =========================================================================
   Warp example — active sessions (PLACEHOLDER)
   =========================================================================
   PLACEHOLDER. Session and device management lands in Warp's Phase 7, which
   adds the warp/sessions/* endpoints, the craft.warp.sessions variable, and the
   SessionInfo model this page will render (a "this device" badge, per-row sign
   out, and "sign out everywhere else"). Until then this file is only the page
   shell so your routing and navigation have something to point at. It renders no
   session data on purpose. Do not wire it up yet.

   When Phase 7 ships, this template will list craft.warp.sessions and post to
   warp/sessions/revoke and warp/sessions/revoke-others (both recent-auth gated).

   Requires a signed-in user ({% requireLogin %} sends guests to the login page).

   This is a copy-in EXAMPLE. Drop it into your project's templates/, wrap it in
   your site layout, and restyle.
   ========================================================================= #}

{% requireLogin %}

<main class="warp-sessions" id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <h1 class="warp-sessions__title">{{ 'Active sessions'|t('warp') }}</h1>

    <p class="warp-sessions__intro">
        {{ 'Managing the devices signed in to your account is coming soon. Check back after this feature ships.'|t('warp') }}
    </p>

    <p class="warp-sessions__actions">
        <a class="warp-link" href="{{ url('/members') }}">{{ 'Back to your account'|t('warp') }}</a>
    </p>
</main>
